+The assessment uses observed publication activity; it does not assume ROA churn or apply a multiplier to aggregate RRDP traffic.
+The September delta sample comes from the RPKIViews raw RRDP archive [RPKIViews-RRDP].
+It contains 6,953 documents across 13 notification hosts, covering complete serial intervals after the first and through the last observations in the 2026-09-30 collector log.
+The collector log's timezone is unspecified.
+The sample contains 190,738 publish elements: 93,357 manifests, 93,265 CRLs, 3,499 ROAs, 545 certificates, and 72 ASPA objects.
+Of these publishes, 189,289 contain a replacement hash; the sample also contains 768 withdrawal elements.
+Repeated publishes are counted, including periodic republication and replacement.
+
+A separate live snapshot sample was captured on 2026-10-27 between 00:16 and 00:19 UTC from all 39 distinct notification URLs at the selected September hosts.
+This October cohort is separate from the September data and does not represent a simultaneous global state.
+All bodies were uncompressed and matched their notifications' SHA-256, session, and serial.
+The 39 snapshot documents contain 569,070 publish elements and total 1,565,796,047 XML bytes.
+A 496-byte text TAL published in the AFRINIC snapshot is included in transfer bytes, excluded from DER totals, and held at its observed size; future TAL contents are outside this model.
+
+| Suite | Sep 30 delta sequence GiB | Oct 27 snapshots once GiB |
+|---|---|---|
+| RSA-2048 | 1.834 | 1.458 |
+| ML-DSA-44 | 2.736 | 4.888 |
+| ML-DSA-65 | 3.131 | 6.426 |
+| ML-DSA-65 + P-256 Composite | 3.164 | 6.556 |
+
+RSA values are captured XML body sizes; PQ values are estimates from the same observed object contents.
+For each publish element, the model changes its base64 length by 4*ceil(new_DER_bytes/3) - 4*ceil(old_DER_bytes/3), retaining the original URI, XML framing, whitespace, and withdrawal elements.
+RSA identity projections reproduce the captured byte totals exactly.
+Snapshot payloads were parsed, without full schema or RPKI resource/path validation.
+
+The snapshot column counts one copy of each selected body for bootstrap or fallback, not recurring traffic.
+The columns cover different dates and must not be added or used to infer a snapshot-to-delta traffic ratio.
+The estimates exclude notifications, compression, HTTP/TLS overhead, retries, polling, client catch-up, and snapshot fallback frequency.
+Neither cohort covers a full quarter or all publication points; no quarterly or all-client traffic total is inferred.
+Equivalent trace-backed rsync and Erik comparisons remain separate work.
+Collection and validation details, exact totals, and retention limits are recorded in [pqc-rpki-lab].
 
